<title>USA: Eastern Co board vote confirmed.</title>
<headline>Eastern Co board vote confirmed.</headline>
<dateline>NAUGATUCK, Conn. 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eastern Co said on Thursday that a final tally of its shareholder vote confirmed that the management's slate of directors defeated a group backed by a dissident shareholder.</p>
<p>Also, a proposal to sell the company was defeated with 60 percent of the shares counted opposing the plan, Eastern Co said.</p>
<p>Each of the management's nominees received at least 1,639,647 shares, or about 70 percent of the votes cast, Eastern Co said.</p>
<p>These results confirm preliminary results that were reported after the March 26 shareholder meeting, the company said.</p>
</text>
